id: pm-web-jstr
title: Ordinary presence join storms fail readiness before 3000 subscribers
description: "Follow-up to pm-web-h4vh. With unchanged production queue, stall, authorization and pool bounds, a sixteen-slot ordinary ramp returned an SSE project-verification HTTP 500 around 1800 subscriptions; an eight-slot diagnostic disconnected readers around 1400 subscriptions. No measured mutations had started in either failed setup. Preserve the failed sequences in docs/capacity/2026-10-20-fanout-exploratory.json. The fan-out comparison defers incremental presence only in its test preload, then requires every real full-roster receipt before measuring established subscribers. This does not certify ordinary join storms. Profile roster generation/transport, membership reads, pool waits and safe verification error categories; repair the ordinary join path without weakening authorization or slow-viewer bounds."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: capacity,performance,realtime
created_at: "2026-10-20T20:43:47.665Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:45:43.808Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Ordinary startup with no quiet-setup control reaches and retains 100, 1000 and 3000 distinct authorized subscribers on one project; every socket receives the complete final roster; mixed committed mutations retain zero loss and duplicates; normal release thresholds and queue/auth bounds remain unchanged."
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T21:13:40.945Z",codex-agent,"The final baseline ordinary ramp also failed before measurement, while the deferred-presence candidate held 3000 subscribers and delivered 150000 mutations exactly. An earlier baseline ordinary ramp succeeded, so readiness remains variable. Corrected test-preload registration order after archiving the data; the source-replacement regression fails on the old order. This only repairs comparison setup control. Production ordinary joining remains unresolved; retain the unchanged authorization, queue/stall and pool bounds in any follow-up."
  "2026-10-21T04:41:48.359Z",codex-agent,"Measuring ordinary authenticated join bursts with the existing disposable capacity fixture, production process and independent SSE readers. Extending the harness to sample readiness during admission and roster convergence for bursts of 100, 500 and 1000 up to 3000 subscribers. No quiet-setup interception; authorization and replay bounds remain required."
  "2026-10-21T04:46:23.462Z",codex-agent,"Exploratory unchanged-server burst-100 run reproduced a setup failure at 1397 opened streams: 41 failed readiness samples (39 HTTP 503, two client deadlines), readiness p99 1858 ms, event-loop p99 257 ms, peak server RSS 279 MiB. This first driver overallocated reader workers; correcting it to reuse four workers before the controlled before/after comparison. Candidate design coalesces roster updates into fixed one-second windows and yields bounded socket batches, refreshing authorization between batches while preserving replay cursors and byte/stall limits."
  "2026-10-21T04:55:23.876Z",codex-agent,"Source-level fan-out and SSE regressions pass 35/35, including fresh membership checks after yielded slices, shared batch identity for 3000 sinks, queue/stall limits, ordered replay, and fresh rosters on resume. The baseline runtime artifacts still exactly match main while measurement runs; production source edits have not been built into that baseline. Shared-host load has exceeded 60 on four logical CPUs, so setup deadlines and latency samples remain explicit limitations, not capacity approval."
  "2026-10-21T05:01:34.797Z",codex-agent,"The controlled 1000-request baseline burst failed project verification before meaningful roster traffic (one opened reader, three readiness deadlines). Join setup now has bounded FIFO admission: up to eight concurrent initializations, reduced for smaller SQL pools, with 4096 pending slots and cancellation on socket close. Each admitted request retains all original authorization and cursor checks. Real HTTP admission regression passes 1/1 for overload, cancellation, idempotent release and responsive readiness."
  "2026-10-21T05:13:09.968Z",codex-agent,"Final 16-slot admission campaign retains healthy readiness in all observed probes but does NOT reach the 3000-subscriber goal. Bursts 100/500/1000 complete cohorts through 2500/1500/1000; opened readers total 2500/1850/1813 before unchanged 15-second connection deadlines. Readiness failures 0/819, 0/217, 0/211; p99 349.5/345.7/309.6 ms. Server loop p99 155.1/153.7/109.4 ms; peak RSS 325.9/338.1/312.5 MiB. No observed disconnections, but no complete 3000-person roster barrier and no capacity approval. Load averages ranged roughly 46-71 on four logical CPUs. Retaining raw aggregate evidence and the earlier eight-slot attempts; no percentage speedup claim."
  "2026-10-21T05:16:49.859Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs succeeded. Reverting only schedulePresence to main and rebuilding makes the real production-process regression fail 0/1: presence population 1 arrived during the coalescing window. Restoring it and reverting only flushFanout to main makes the same real-process regression fail 0/1 on the bounded socket-slice assertion. Disabling only the admission concurrency branch makes the real HTTP admission test fail 0/1: four initializations enter a two-slot gate. Every changed source was restored byte-for-byte after each proof."
  "2026-10-21T05:22:10.410Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation passes PM-linked focused checks: 40/40 real-process, fan-out, SSE delivery and recovery tests, plus 1/1 real HTTP admission test; zero skipped/canceled. Lint passes, duplication is 0% (0 clone pairs), and docstring gate passes. The project disables automatic test-result tracking, so pm test returned tracking_disabled; this public-safe comment and the dated report retain the results without storing raw execution contexts."
  "2026-10-21T05:36:15.104Z",codex-agent,"Checkpoint for orchestrator: implementation, public aggregate measurements and three behavioral revert proofs are retained. PM-linked checks pass 40/40 plus 1/1; lint, zero-duplication and docstrings pass. Full npm release:check is still executing with isolated HOME/Git identity and has no final verdict. Bun release:check has not run. The measured 3000-subscriber goal remains unmet: final observed complete cohorts 2500/1500/1000 for bursts 100/500/1000, with zero failed readiness samples in those three attempts. Remaining work: finish both release gates, repeat measurements against the final built artifacts after lint-only changes, update the report and open the PR. No PR, merge or release has occurred."
  "2026-10-21T05:41:54.486Z",codex-agent,"Resumed final verification. The earlier npm release gate ended without a final verdict; rerunning it, then running the Bun gate at unchanged thresholds. Retaining completed measurements and revert proofs. The PR will explicitly report the unmet 3000-subscriber target and measured limits per burst size."
  "2026-10-21T06:07:27.557Z",codex-agent,"The resumed full npm gate has passed type checking, lint, zero duplication and docstrings; its serial coverage suite is still running. It has reported a 300-second built catalog timeout, a source catalog failure, and a large-corpus graph wall-time bound failure. Retaining every verdict and unchanged thresholds; the exact final counts and Bun result will follow. The completed join-storm campaign is not being repeated after equivalent lint-only spelling changes, which are now called out in the dated report."
  "2026-10-21T06:21:57.619Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm release:check exited 1 at coverage: 761 tests, 758 pass, two fail, one canceled, zero skipped. Built catalog install hit its unchanged 300-second deadline; source catalog listing then reported spawn ENOTDIR; the 2000-item graph read took 11467 ms against 10000 ms. Aggregate statements/lines 92.10%, branches 82.47%, functions 95.97% exceed unchanged thresholds, but failed tests keep the gate red and later release stages did not run. The new real-process join regression and admission/fan-out/SSE cases passed in this run. Existing pm-web-qdhx and pm-web-hqqp cover related timing investigations. The full Bun gate is now running."
  "2026-10-21T07:07:55.275Z",codex-agent,"The full Bun gate is still running. Its new production-process join regression has passed, as have admission/fan-out/SSE checks. Reported failures so far are the two catalog cases, graph wall budget at 13451 ms, graph provisioning returning HTTP 424, and the existing independent-workspace spawn overlap assertion. Retaining all of them; no deadline, exclusion or coverage threshold changes. Final counts and wrapper exit are pending."
  "2026-10-21T07:13:50.546Z",codex-agent,"Final required gates are red at unchanged coverage thresholds. npm run release:check exited 1: 758 pass, two fail, one canceled of 761, zero skipped; Bun exited 1: 756 pass, four fail, one canceled of 761, zero skipped. Aggregate coverage npm statements/lines 92.10, branches 82.47, functions 95.97; Bun 92.36, 82.24, 95.97 percent. Both passed the changed production-process, admission, fan-out and SSE regressions. Catalog timing/ENOTDIR, graph wall budget, provisioning activation timeout and spawn overlap evidence enrich pm-web-qdhx, pm-web-hqqp and pm-web-jpa6. Both command chains stop before later release stages. No code/test changes between gates. Preparing a draft PR: 3000 target unmet, completed cohorts 2500/1500/1000 for bursts 100/500/1000, with 0/1247 readiness failures in the measured sixteen-slot campaign. Report includes measured-versus-committed runtime hashes and the lint-only difference; no campaign rerun or capacity approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-21T07:17:33.148Z",codex-agent,"Opened draft PR #234: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/234 . Implementation commit 0a15d78; measurement and gate receipt commit 0bf9b28. The PR explicitly reports the unmet 3000-subscriber target, complete cohorts 2500/1500/1000 by burst size, zero observed readiness failures in the measured sixteen-slot campaign, and failed full npm/Bun gates. Three behavioral revert proofs and restored focused checks remain documented. No merge or release. Releasing the claim with the item still in progress for further admission profiling and gate investigations."
  "2026-10-21T07:51:10.050Z",codex-agent,"PR #234 review round: fetched all review threads and their comments (one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uqz62; no pagination omissions); latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. Remote branch is current and contains main. Verified the later-slice authorization failure incorrectly detaches processed viewers and late registrations. Restrict failure cleanup to the current and remaining snapshot slices, add behavioral regressions and revert proofs, self-review the full PR, rebuild committed output, then execute unchanged npm and Bun release gates. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T07:52:39.532Z",codex-agent,"Review fix and revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uqz62: flushFanout now retains the current slice and detaches only it and the remaining finite snapshot on authorization failure. Self-reviewed the full PR for snapshot/registration boundaries, membership failures, backpressure cleanup, admission cancellation, and worker receipt handling; no additional instance of this defect found. node --test test/sse-fanout.test.ts passes 21/21. Reverting only flushFanout to the pre-review implementation while keeping both new tests makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"an authorization failure in slice\" test/sse-fanout.test.ts fail 0/2 (exit 1): 97 closes versus expected 64 for slice 2 and 32 for slice 3. This proves both processed viewers and post-snapshot joins were incorrectly detached. Restored the fixed source byte-for-byte. Tests also verify listener cleanup, no private delivery to failed slices, and ordered recovery of surviving connections."
  "2026-10-21T07:53:46.458Z",codex-agent,"Restored PM-linked checks pass: 42/42 production-process, fan-out, SSE delivery and recovery checks; 1/1 real HTTP admission test; 21/21 standalone fan-out checks. Zero failures/skips/cancellations in all three commands. The pinned tracker reports tracking_disabled, so these public-safe comments retain counts rather than enabling raw execution-context recording. Dependency installation initially failed because host npm user configuration passed allow-scripts into a git dependency preparation; retry with npm_config_userconfig and NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG set to the null device succeeded without repository changes. Starting full isolated-identity npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T08:07:04.180Z",codex-agent,"Verification continuation: transient provider interruption stopped the first npm gate during the source catalog acceptance, before a final verdict. Its built catalog case passed in 242.4 seconds at the unchanged 300-second bound. Retaining that partial receipt; restarting the incomplete full gate and sequencing the Bun gate after it. Repository CI setup script refreshed the ignored managed extension; pinned strict health with required merge drivers now passes, including history drift and integrity, with only the existing stale-item advisory. No further code changes."
  "2026-10-21T08:37:17.847Z",codex-agent,"Review-round full isolated-identity npm run release:check exited 1 at coverage: 763 tests, 761 pass, one fail, one canceled, zero skipped. Aggregate statements/lines 92.31%, branches 82.24%, functions 95.97%, above unchanged 92.07/80.5/94.59 thresholds. The built catalog case hit its unchanged 300-second deadline; the source case then returned spawn ENOTDIR instead of the inactive-package refusal. The same fixed built catalog case passed in 242.4 seconds in the interrupted attempt. Changed production-process joins, admission, both new slice-failure regressions and all fan-out/SSE checks pass. Graph budget passes at 8868 ms against 10000 ms; graph provisioning and spawn overlap pass. Static gates pass, duplication 0%. Later release stages did not run in this command chain. Full Bun gate is running; no code changes between them."
  "2026-10-21T09:08:05.010Z",codex-agent,"Review-round isolated bun run release:check exited 1 at coverage: 763 tests, 760 pass, two fail, one canceled, zero skipped. Statements/lines 92.34%, branches 82.41%, functions 95.68%, all above unchanged thresholds. Catalog built case reaches 300 seconds; source install then reports spawn ENOTDIR. Existing spawn fallback overlap assertion also fails (it passed in the completed npm gate). Both new slice-failure regressions, production-process join/admission/fan-out/SSE, graph provisioning, and graph budget pass. Graph wall 6589 ms against unchanged 10000 ms. No executable source or test changes between full gates. Running isolated catalog and spawn retries plus remaining release stages independently because both full chains stop at coverage."
  "2026-10-21T09:24:09.887Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round receipt: refreshed all review threads/comments again; only PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6uqz62 remains and the latest review has no Outside diff range findings. Valid finding fixed, full PR self-reviewed for related snapshot/cleanup defects with no additional instance found. Behavioral revert fails 0/2, restored fan-out passes 21/21; PM-linked checks pass 42/42 plus admission 1/1. Full npm and Bun release checks stop at coverage with counts and unchanged-threshold coverage recorded above; catalog retry remains 1/3 (one fail, one canceled), while spawn-overlap retry passes 1/1. All seven later release stages pass independently: capacity 2/2; production audit zero vulnerabilities; package dry-run; packed npm/native-Bun current/minimum consumers 4/4; changelog check; release-date check; publish-attestation check. docs/capacity/2026-10-21-joinstorm.md preserves both historical and review-round results. Committed output rebuilt. Source SHA-256 3c3c7e8d4810cc7800faf3899637fbf5dffb46dd5cda591d271ea588f51887d0; built fan-out SHA-256 be7117d9932559246604ce18f8d5e9f34dae7dc84a51eb1fd05f1631401720f5; regression SHA-256 9e64a73c7d78aa5cbb053c9f1700b692762bdba3bc92b642b15fc7ec29baa5d1. Remaining risks: catalog validation gaps and unmet 3000-subscriber capacity target. Leaving in progress and releasing the claim; no thread replies/resolutions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-24T21:45:43.808Z",codex-agent,"Returned to open in the 2026-10-24 sweep: Open PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/239 explicitly leaves the ordinary 3000-subscriber readiness target unmet. The full final-roster, zero-loss/duplicate ordinary-startup acceptance is not established; no active agent is established."
